    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change is small, additive, and follows the existing shape of the file. A few specifics:\n\n- The new length rule is factored into a dedicated private helper (`hasValidNationalLength`) rather than inlined into `normalize`, which keeps `normalize` reading as a sequence of guard clauses (`< 8 || > 15`, then the country-specific check). That's the right unit \u2014 the generic length check and the per-country check stay separate concerns.\n- The helper is placed directly after `normalize`, named with the verb-phrase convention used elsewhere, and carries Javadoc consistent with the method it supports. The class `Javadoc` was also updated to describe the new behavior, so the documentation stays coherent with the code.\n- Nothing is duplicated \u2014 the 8\u201315 digit bound isn't repeated, and the country logic lives in one place.\n- Writing the checks as `length - 2 == 9` / `length - 1 == 10` (country-code length subtracted, then national length asserted) mirrors the spec's phrasing (\"national number must have N digits\"), which a maintainer adding a third country would find natural to extend.\n\nNo structural improvements needed for the scope of this diff.",
